  "id": "COMPOUND:17155 - PROTEIN:5811",
  "verbalization": "Undecanol is linked to VMRC-LCP through a series of molecular interactions involving Raji cells, which are targeted by multiple compounds, including (5R,7S,8S)-5-hydroxy-4-methoxy-7,8-dimethyl-7,8-dihydro-5H-pyrano[4,3-b]pyran-2-one, Marsdenoside K, and Glycitein. These compounds all share a common target of Raji cells, suggesting a potential pathway where Undecanol may influence Raji cell function through these intermediates. The evidence suggests that Undecanol could act as a modulator or regulator of the biological processes that lead to the activation of VMRC-LCP in Raji cells. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Undecanol indirectly affects VMRC-LCP through its interaction with Raji cells, potentially by influencing the expression or activity of the target compounds. This relationship underscores the role of Raji cells as a central node in the network of interactions involving Undecanol and VMRC-LCP.",
